==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|acceptour||obsolete|rare}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|acceptour}}, from {{der|en|la|acceptor}}, with the meanings from {{m|en|accept}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əkˈsɛptə(ɹ)/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/əkˈsɛp.tɚ/|/ækˈsɛp.tɚ/|a=GenAm}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-acceptor.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[accept]]s.
# {{lb|en|legal|commerce}} One who accepts a draft or a bill of exchange; a [[drawee]] after he has accepted.
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} An [[atom]] or [[molecule]] which can accept an [[electron]] to form a chemical [[bond]].
# {{lb|en|biochemistry}} A [[transfer RNA]] molecule that can accept a specific [[amino acid]]
# {{lb|en|physics}} A chemical acceptor atom forming a positive hole in a semiconductor
# {{lb|en|physiology}} A cluster of [[skin]] [[cell]]s that respond to [[pain]]
# {{lb|en|comptheory}} A kind of [[finite-state machine]] whose [[binary]] [[output]] indicates whether or not a received [[input]] was accepted.

